---
device: Line 6 HX Effects
manufacturer: Line 6
version: 3.80
default_channel: 1
documentation: https://line6.com/support/manuals/hxeffects
firmware_notes: |
  HX EFFECTS: EFFECTS-ONLY PROCESSOR
  - 4 SNAPSHOTS per preset (same as HX Stomp XL)
  - 6 FOOTSWITCHES (FS1-6)
  - 2 EXPRESSION PEDALS (EXP1, EXP2)
  - 5-PIN DIN MIDI (full MIDI In/Out/Thru) - ADVANTAGE over HX Stomp/XL
  - Full Command Center (no CV/Ext Amp - effects only)
  - Effects processing only (no amp/cab modeling)
  
  UNIQUE PRESET ADDRESSING:
  - 128 presets organized as 32 Banks × 4 Presets (A-D)
  - PC 0-3   = Bank 1 Presets A-D
  - PC 4-7   = Bank 2 Presets A-D
  - PC 124-127 = Bank 32 Presets A-D
  - Sequential addressing (no Bank Select needed)
  
  TIMING REQUIREMENTS:
  - Same as other Helix: 350ms after PC (firmware 3.5x), 50ms for 3.10+
---

# ============================================
# PRESET MANAGEMENT - UNIQUE ADDRESSING
# ============================================

# HX Effects uses SEQUENTIAL PRESET ADDRESSING
# Different from both full Helix (CC32+PC) and HX Stomp (direct PC)
# 
# Preset Organization:
# Bank 1:  PC 0=A, PC 1=B, PC 2=C, PC 3=D
# Bank 2:  PC 4=A, PC 5=B, PC 6=C, PC 7=D
# Bank 3:  PC 8=A, PC 9=B, PC 10=C, PC 11=D
# ...
# Bank 32: PC 124=A, PC 125=B, PC 126=C, PC 127=D

# Direct preset addressing
@alias hxfx_preset pc.{ch}.{preset:0-127} "Load preset (0-127)"

# Bank-based addressing helper (converts bank + preset letter to PC number)
@alias hxfx_bank_preset {ch} {bank:1-32} {preset=a:0,b:1,c:2,d:3} "Load preset by bank and letter"
  # Calculate PC number: ((bank - 1) * 4) + preset_offset
  # This is a conceptual alias - actual implementation would need expression evaluation
  # For now, users should calculate: Bank N Preset A = PC (N-1)*4
  - pc {ch}.{preset}
@end

# Named preset shortcuts for first bank (commonly used)
@alias hxfx_bank1_a pc.{ch}.0 "Bank 1 Preset A"
@alias hxfx_bank1_b pc.{ch}.1 "Bank 1 Preset B"
@alias hxfx_bank1_c pc.{ch}.2 "Bank 1 Preset C"
@alias hxfx_bank1_d pc.{ch}.3 "Bank 1 Preset D"

# Preset Navigation (moves by 1 preset)
@alias hxfx_next_preset cc.{ch}.72.127 "Next preset (A→B→C→D→next bank A→...)"
@alias hxfx_prev_preset cc.{ch}.72.0 "Previous preset"

# Combined preset + snapshot load
@alias hxfx_load_snapshot {ch} {preset:0-127} {snapshot:0-3} "Load preset and switch to snapshot"
  - pc {ch}.{preset}
  [+350ms]
  - cc {ch}.69.{snapshot}
@end

# ============================================
# PRESET ADDRESSING CALCULATOR
# ============================================

# Quick reference for calculating PC numbers:
# Bank 1:  PC 0-3    (Presets A-D)
# Bank 2:  PC 4-7
# Bank 3:  PC 8-11
# Bank 4:  PC 12-15
# Bank 5:  PC 16-19
# Bank 6:  PC 20-23
# Bank 7:  PC 24-27
# Bank 8:  PC 28-31
# Bank 9:  PC 32-35
# Bank 10: PC 36-39
# ...
# Bank 32: PC 124-127

# Formula: PC = ((Bank - 1) × 4) + Preset_Offset
# Where Preset_Offset: A=0, B=1, C=2, D=3

# Examples:
# Bank 5 Preset C  = ((5-1) × 4) + 2 = 18
# Bank 10 Preset A = ((10-1) × 4) + 0 = 36
# Bank 15 Preset D = ((15-1) × 4) + 3 = 59

# ============================================
# SNAPSHOT CONTROL
# ============================================

# HX Effects has 4 SNAPSHOTS (0-3) - same as HX Stomp XL
@alias hxfx_snapshot cc.{ch}.69.{snap:0-3} "Switch to snapshot (0=Snap1...3=Snap4)"

# Named snapshot shortcuts
@alias hxfx_snap_1 cc.{ch}.69.0 "Snapshot 1"
@alias hxfx_snap_2 cc.{ch}.69.1 "Snapshot 2"
@alias hxfx_snap_3 cc.{ch}.69.2 "Snapshot 3"
@alias hxfx_snap_4 cc.{ch}.69.3 "Snapshot 4"

# Snapshot Navigation
@alias hxfx_snap_next cc.{ch}.69.8 "Next snapshot (wraps: 4→1)"
@alias hxfx_snap_prev cc.{ch}.69.9 "Previous snapshot (wraps: 1→4)"

# ============================================
# EXPRESSION PEDAL EMULATION
# ============================================

@alias hxfx_exp1 cc.{ch}.1.{value:0-127} "Emulate EXP 1 pedal position"
@alias hxfx_exp2 cc.{ch}.2.{value:0-127} "Emulate EXP 2 pedal position"

# Expression toe switch
@alias hxfx_exp_toe cc.{ch}.59.{state:0-127} "EXP toe switch (0-63=off, 64-127=on)"
@alias hxfx_exp_toe_on cc.{ch}.59.127 "EXP toe switch on"
@alias hxfx_exp_toe_off cc.{ch}.59.0 "EXP toe switch off"

# ============================================
# FOOTSWITCH EMULATION
# ============================================

# HX Effects has 6 FOOTSWITCHES (FS1-6)
# NOTE: Looper documentation references different footswitch numbers (FS3, FS6)
# These are the physical footswitch labels, not CC numbers

@alias hxfx_fs1 cc.{ch}.49.127 "Toggle Footswitch 1"
@alias hxfx_fs2 cc.{ch}.50.127 "Toggle Footswitch 2"
@alias hxfx_fs3 cc.{ch}.51.127 "Toggle Footswitch 3"
@alias hxfx_fs4 cc.{ch}.52.127 "Toggle Footswitch 4"
@alias hxfx_fs5 cc.{ch}.53.127 "Toggle Footswitch 5"
@alias hxfx_fs6 cc.{ch}.54.127 "Toggle Footswitch 6"

# Generic footswitch control
@alias hxfx_footswitch cc.{ch}.{fs_cc:49-54}.{value:0-127} "Control any footswitch (FS1=49...FS6=54)"

# ============================================
# LOOPER CONTROL
# ============================================

# HX Effects looper CCs are same as other models but with different
# footswitch references in documentation (FS3, FS6 vs FS1, FS2)

@alias hxfx_looper_record cc.{ch}.60.{mode=overdub:0,record:127} "Record/Overdub mode"
@alias hxfx_looper_record_overdub cc.{ch}.60.0 "Set looper to overdub mode"
@alias hxfx_looper_record_rec cc.{ch}.60.127 "Set looper to record mode"

@alias hxfx_looper_play_stop cc.{ch}.61.{state=stop:0,play:127} "Play/Stop control"
@alias hxfx_looper_play cc.{ch}.61.127 "Play looper"
@alias hxfx_looper_stop cc.{ch}.61.0 "Stop looper"

# Play Once corresponds to physical FS6 on HX Effects
@alias hxfx_looper_play_once cc.{ch}.62.127 "Play once (one-shot playback, FS6)"

# Undo/Redo corresponds to physical FS3 on HX Effects
@alias hxfx_looper_undo_redo cc.{ch}.63.127 "Undo/Redo last action (FS3)"

@alias hxfx_looper_direction cc.{ch}.65.{dir=forward:0,reverse:127} "Playback direction"
@alias hxfx_looper_forward cc.{ch}.65.0 "Forward playback"
@alias hxfx_looper_reverse cc.{ch}.65.127 "Reverse playback"

@alias hxfx_looper_speed cc.{ch}.66.{speed=full:0,half:127} "Playback speed"
@alias hxfx_looper_full_speed cc.{ch}.66.0 "Full speed playback"
@alias hxfx_looper_half_speed cc.{ch}.66.127 "Half speed playback"

@alias hxfx_looper_onoff cc.{ch}.67.{state=off:0,on:127} "Looper on/off"
@alias hxfx_looper_on cc.{ch}.67.127 "Enable looper mode"
@alias hxfx_looper_off cc.{ch}.67.0 "Exit looper mode"

# ============================================
# GLOBAL FUNCTIONS
# ============================================

@alias hxfx_tap cc.{ch}.64.127 "Tap tempo"

@alias hxfx_tuner cc.{ch}.68.{state=off:0,on:127} "Tuner on/off"
@alias hxfx_tuner_on cc.{ch}.68.127 "Enable tuner"
@alias hxfx_tuner_off cc.{ch}.68.0 "Disable tuner"

# ============================================
# EFFECTS-ONLY WORKFLOW CONSIDERATIONS
# ============================================

# HX Effects is designed for integration with existing amp rigs
# Key differences from full Helix:
# - NO amp/cab modeling (effects processing only)
# - NO External Amp switching (no Ext Amp Command Center option)
# - NO CV Out (Command Center limitation)
# - HAS 5-pin DIN MIDI (advantage over HX Stomp/XL)
# - HAS full Command Center (PC, CC, CC Toggle, Note, MMC)

# Typical use case: Place HX Effects in amp's effects loop
# - Pre-amp effects (comp, drive, EQ) before amp input
# - Post-amp effects (delay, reverb, mod) in amp's FX loop
# - Control amp channel via Command Center MIDI

# ============================================
# COMMAND CENTER FOR AMP INTEGRATION
# ============================================

# HX Effects excels at controlling external amps via MIDI
# Full Command Center without amp modeling means focus on integration

# Example: Change preset and switch amp channel simultaneously
@alias hxfx_preset_with_amp {ch} {preset:0-127} {amp_channel} "Load HX Effects preset and switch amp channel"
  - pc {ch}.{preset}
  [+350ms]
  # Switch external amp (example: Mesa Boogie on channel 2)
  - pc 2.{amp_channel}
@end

# Example: Snapshot change with amp channel switch
@alias hxfx_snapshot_with_amp {ch} {snapshot:0-3} {amp_channel} "Change snapshot and amp channel"
  - cc {ch}.69.{snapshot}
  [+50ms]
  # Switch amp channel
  - pc 2.{amp_channel}
@end

# Example: Toggle external pedal on snapshot change
@alias hxfx_snapshot_with_pedal {ch} {snapshot:0-3} {pedal_cc} {pedal_state} "Snapshot + external pedal control"
  - cc {ch}.69.{snapshot}
  [+50ms]
  - cc 2.{pedal_cc} {pedal_state}
@end

# ============================================
# 4-SNAPSHOT EFFECTS COMBINATIONS
# ============================================

# With 4 snapshots and effects-only focus, organize by effect layers

# Pattern 1: Dry → Subtle → Wet → Ambient
@alias hxfx_wetness_progression {ch} {preset} "Progressive wetness: dry to ambient"
  - pc {ch}.{preset}
  # Snapshot 1: Dry (minimal FX, amp tone focus)
  # Snapshot 2: Subtle (light delay/reverb)
  # Snapshot 3: Wet (moderate FX mix)
  # Snapshot 4: Ambient (heavy delay/reverb/mod)
@end

# Pattern 2: Clean → Compressed → Driven → Lead
@alias hxfx_pre_amp_stages {ch} {preset} "Pre-amp effect staging"
  - pc {ch}.{preset}
  # Snapshot 1: Clean (comp + EQ only)
  # Snapshot 2: Compressed (comp + light OD)
  # Snapshot 3: Driven (comp + medium drive)
  # Snapshot 4: Lead (comp + boost + drive)
@end

# Pattern 3: Verse → Chorus → Bridge → Solo (song sections)
@alias hxfx_song_sections {ch} {preset} "Song section presets"
  - pc {ch}.{preset}
  # Snapshot 1: Verse FX
  # Snapshot 2: Chorus FX
  # Snapshot 3: Bridge FX
  # Snapshot 4: Solo FX
@end

# ============================================
# COMPLETE SONG WITH AMP INTEGRATION
# ============================================

# This macro demonstrates HX Effects controlling both its own effects
# and an external MIDI-capable amp

@alias hxfx_complete_song {ch} {song_preset} {amp_channel_verse} {amp_channel_chorus} {amp_channel_lead} "Full song: HX Effects + Amp control"
  # INTRO - Clean amp, subtle effects
  # [00:00.000]
  - pc {ch}.{song_preset}
  [+350ms]
  - cc {ch}.69.0              # HX Effects Snapshot 1 (subtle)
  [@]
  - pc 2.{amp_channel_verse}  # Amp clean channel
  
  # VERSE - Same effects, maybe different amp voice
  # [00:16.000]
  - cc {ch}.69.1              # HX Effects Snapshot 2 (verse FX)
  # Amp stays on clean/verse channel
  
  # PRE-CHORUS - Add effects, prepare for amp channel change
  # [00:28.000]
  - cc {ch}.69.2              # HX Effects Snapshot 3 (build FX)
  
  # CHORUS - Switch amp to gain channel, moderate effects
  # [00:32.000]
  - cc {ch}.69.2              # HX Effects Snapshot 3 (chorus FX)
  [@]
  - pc 2.{amp_channel_chorus} # Amp gain channel
  
  # VERSE 2 - Back to clean amp
  # [00:48.000]
  - cc {ch}.69.1              # HX Effects Snapshot 2
  [@]
  - pc 2.{amp_channel_verse}  # Amp clean channel
  
  # BRIDGE - Different effects, maybe different amp setting
  # [01:04.000]
  - cc {ch}.69.3              # HX Effects Snapshot 4 (ambient)
  [@]
  - pc 2.{amp_channel_verse}  # Keep amp clean for contrast
  
  # SOLO - Lead amp channel, lead effects
  # [01:20.000]
  - cc {ch}.69.4              # HX Effects Snapshot 4 (lead FX)
  [@]
  - pc 2.{amp_channel_lead}   # Amp lead channel
  
  # FINAL CHORUS - High energy
  # [01:36.000]
  - cc {ch}.69.2              # HX Effects Snapshot 3
  [@]
  - pc 2.{amp_channel_chorus} # Amp gain channel
  
  # OUTRO - Return to clean
  # [01:52.000]
  - cc {ch}.69.0              # HX Effects Snapshot 1
  [@]
  - pc 2.{amp_channel_verse}  # Amp clean channel
@end

# ============================================
# 5-PIN DIN MIDI ADVANTAGES
# ============================================

# HX Effects has 5-pin DIN MIDI (unlike HX Stomp/XL)
# This enables:
# - Hardware MIDI Thru for daisy-chaining devices
# - Lower jitter for MIDI Clock (vs USB)
# - Optical isolation (no ground loops)
# - Standard MIDI controller compatibility
# - No computer/USB host required

# Typical MIDI chain:
# MIDI Controller → HX Effects → External Amp → External Pedals
#     (5-pin DIN)      THRU         THRU            END

# Configure MIDI Thru in Global Settings > MIDI/Tempo > MIDI Thru

# ============================================
# EXPRESSION PEDAL FOR AMP CHANNEL VOLUME
# ============================================

# HX Effects can control external gear via expression pedals
# Example: Control amp's solo volume via expression pedal

# NOTE: This alias is commented out because @sweep with ramp() syntax is not yet fully implemented
# Uncomment when sweep/ramp functionality is complete
#
# @alias hxfx_exp_amp_solo {ch} {exp_cc} {min_vol} {max_vol} "Expression controls amp solo volume"
#   # This requires the amp to respond to a specific CC for volume
#   # Configure expression pedal to send that CC with appropriate range
#
#   # In HX Effects: assign EXP1 to send CC (via Command Center)
#   # Then sweep the expression pedal:
#   @sweep from [00:00.000] to [00:04.000] every 16t
#     - cc 2.{exp_cc} ramp({min_vol}, {max_vol})
#   @end
# @end

# ============================================
# BANK ORGANIZATION STRATEGIES
# ============================================

# With 32 Banks × 4 Presets, organize logically:

# Strategy 1: By Song (one bank per song)
# Bank 1 (PC 0-3):   Song 1 - Intro, Verse, Chorus, Bridge
# Bank 2 (PC 4-7):   Song 2 - Intro, Verse, Chorus, Bridge
# Bank 3 (PC 8-11):  Song 3 - Intro, Verse, Chorus, Bridge
# ...

# Strategy 2: By Effect Type
# Bank 1 (PC 0-3):   Delay-focused presets (A-D variations)
# Bank 2 (PC 4-7):   Reverb-focused presets
# Bank 3 (PC 8-11):  Modulation-focused presets
# Bank 4 (PC 12-15): Drive-focused presets
# ...

# Strategy 3: By Setlist
# Bank 1-4 (PC 0-15):    Set 1 songs (4 presets × 4 songs)
# Bank 5-8 (PC 16-31):   Set 2 songs
# Bank 9-12 (PC 32-47):  Set 3 songs
# ...

# Strategy 4: By Amp Channel Pairing
# Bank 1 (PC 0-3):   Clean amp channel effects (A-D variations)
# Bank 2 (PC 4-7):   Crunch amp channel effects
# Bank 3 (PC 8-11):  Lead amp channel effects
# Bank 4 (PC 12-15): Specialty sounds
# ...

# ============================================
# USAGE EXAMPLES
# ============================================

# Example 1: Load specific bank/preset
# [00:00.000]
# - hxfx_preset 1 18              // Bank 5 Preset C: ((5-1)×4)+2 = 18

# Example 2: Song with snapshots
# [00:00.000]
# - hxfx_preset 1 8               // Bank 3 Preset A
# [00:16.000]
# - hxfx_snap_2 1                 // Verse
# [00:32.000]
# - hxfx_snap_3 1                 // Chorus
# [00:48.000]
# - hxfx_snap_4 1                 // Bridge

# Example 3: Expression automation
# @sweep from [00:00.000] to [00:08.000] every 16t
#   - hxfx_exp1 1 ramp(0, 127)
# @end

# Example 4: Preset with amp channel change
# [01:00.000]
# - hxfx_preset_with_amp 1 12 2  // Bank 4 Preset A, Amp Channel 2

# Example 5: Footswitch toggles
# [01:30.000]
# - hxfx_fs1 1                    // Toggle delay
# [01:32.000]
# - hxfx_fs2 1                    // Toggle reverb
# [01:34.000]
# - hxfx_fs3 1                    // Toggle modulation

# ============================================
# COMPATIBLE AMPS AND CONTROLLERS
# ============================================

# MIDI-Capable Amps (can be controlled via HX Effects):
# - Mesa Boogie Mark series (channel switching)
# - Marshall JVM series (channel + FX loop)
# - Peavey 6505+ (channel switching)
# - Hughes & Kettner (comprehensive MIDI)
# - Bogner (some models)
# - Friedman (some models)
# - Victory amps (MIDI jack)

# Popular MIDI Controllers for HX Effects:
# - Morningstar MC6/MC6 Pro/MC8 (excellent integration)
# - Disaster Area Designs controllers (DMC series)
# - RJM Music Mastermind series
# - Voes controllers
# - MIDI Solutions foot controllers

# ============================================
# RESERVED CC NUMBERS
# ============================================

# DO NOT use these for custom parameter control:
# CC1   - Expression Pedal 1
# CC2   - Expression Pedal 2
# CC49-54 - Footswitches 1-6
# CC59  - EXP Toe Switch
# CC60-67 - Looper controls
# CC64  - Tap Tempo
# CC68  - Tuner
# CC69  - Snapshot Select
# CC72  - Preset Navigation
# CC73-76 - Reserved

# All other CCs available for MIDI Learn

# ============================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING
# ============================================

# Issue: "Confused by preset numbering"
# Solution: Remember formula: PC = ((Bank-1) × 4) + Preset_Offset
#          Bank 1 = PC 0-3, Bank 2 = PC 4-7, etc.
#          Use calculator chart above

# Issue: "Amp doesn't respond to MIDI"
# Solution: Check amp's MIDI channel matches HX Effects
#          Verify amp has MIDI enabled (check amp manual)
#          Test with MIDI monitor to confirm messages sent
#          Some amps require specific MIDI implementation

# Issue: "MIDI Thru not working"
# Solution: Enable in Global Settings > MIDI/Tempo > MIDI Thru
#          Firmware 3.71+ required for proper Thru implementation
#          Check MIDI cable connections

# Issue: "4 snapshots not enough"
# Solution: Use presets (32 banks × 4 = 128 total)
#          Organize by song/section rather than tone variations
#          Consider full Helix if need 8 snapshots

# Issue: "Need CV output"
# Solution: HX Effects lacks CV Out (effects-only design)
#          Use full Helix Floor/Rack for CV capability
#          Or use external MIDI-to-CV converter

# Issue: "Expression pedal sluggish"
# Solution: Calibrate in Global Settings
#          Check expression pedal cable connection
#          Verify pedal resistance (10K-25K required)
#          Use expression pedal polarity setting if needed
